# Packages for the s3-garage flavor (single-node Garage, objects on the NVMe).
#
# Deliberately NO S3 server package: Garage is not in Fedora and upstream ships
# it as a container, which podman + Quadlet run from
# /usr/share/containers/systemd/. podman itself is already in the base image.
#
# No `attr` here, unlike the s3-versity flavor: Garage stores object metadata in
# its own database, not in filesystem extended attributes.

# --- Storage for the object volume ---------------------------------------
xfsprogs # REQUIRED: systemd-makefs shells out to mkfs.xfs to format the NVMe
util-linux # blkid guards the format step; lsblk to see what is actually there

# --- NVMe / disk tooling -------------------------------------------------
nvme-cli # namespace/format/smart-log for the object drive
smartmontools # SMART health — the objects have no redundancy, watch the disk

# --- Talking to the S3 endpoint from the box itself ----------------------
awscli2 # the obvious smoke test: aws --endpoint-url http://localhost:9000 s3 ls

# --- Diagnostics ---------------------------------------------------------
iotop
sysstat # iostat, mpstat, sar
